Idealised trend for a cubic graph of girth g whose typical pairs are at distance >= g/2:  cone ratio -> 4 / (2 - 2 cos(2 pi/g)) ~ g^2/pi^2,
against the Ramanujan value 1/(1 - 2 sqrt2/3) = 17.49 for the Euclidean constant.  Crossover near g = 13.
